## 1. Open Source License — GNU AGPLv3

If you are developing open-source software, performing academic research, or
are willing to open-source your entire application's source code under the
AGPLv3, you may use Balansis for free.

**Crucial Condition:** According to the AGPLv3, if you modify Balansis or
integrate it into a software system that interacts with users remotely over a
network (e.g., cloud services, SaaS, AI/ML web-services, REST APIs), you
**MUST make your entire system's source code available to the public** under
the AGPLv3 license.

See `LICENSE-AGPLv3` for the full legal text.

---

## 2. Commercial / Enterprise License

If you wish to integrate Balansis into proprietary software, commercial
products, internal enterprise platforms, closed-source SaaS applications, or
revenue-generating AI/ML production pipelines where you **cannot or do not
want to disclose your source code**, you CANNOT use the AGPLv3 version.

In this case, you **must purchase a Commercial License** from the copyright
holder.

The Commercial License grants you the right to:
- Keep your source code private
- Deploy Balansis in commercial and production environments
- Receive production stability warranties and priority support

For commercial licensing terms, pricing, and enterprise agreements:

  **Email:** andrew@xteam.pro
